    "difficultyReason": "Part a needs rearrangement to cos θ = 1/2, then a reference angle and the Q1/Q4 solutions. Part b uses the boundary value cos θ = -1, which has a single solution. Part c is heavily scaffolded: the student splits the product and reuses the answers from a and b. The hardest demand is a routine two-quadrant trig solve, below the multi-stage reasoning in p68-q7.",
